weaknesses.value:
1. The contribution of the proposed method is restricted to the combination of two established robust training techniques with an existing MLX approach;

2. Although the authors thoroughly review various regularization-based MLX approaches in the introduction, the paper only showcases the effectiveness of combining robust training methods with a single MLX approach, Grad-Reg. It remains unclear whether the proposed approach can be applied to other MLX methods, and further investigation is necessary to determine its generalizability.

In addition, Table 1 does not include the results of the more recent MLX approaches that are well discussed in the introduction section.

